 ### Late Viewing Direction Conditioning
-A design choice to fuse the viewing direction only in the last layer of the color MLP [S2]. This prevents the optimization from bypassing the neural voxel to learn a direct mapping from viewing direction to output sample color, which leads to erroneous camera poses and geometry [S2]. Without late viewing direction conditioning, the optimization could minimize photometric loss by optimizing the MLP directly, leading to erroneous camera poses and geometry estimation [S2]. Choose it to prevent erroneous camera poses and geometry during optimization.
